# Change files

Every pull request that changes the library or the terminal app adds a
Markdown file to this directory. Knope reads the files to choose the next
version, write `CHANGELOG.md` and open the release pull request. Merging that
pull request publishes the package and the terminal app. The files are deleted
when the release is prepared.

Create one with `knope document-change` (the dev shell provides `knope`), or
write it by hand:

```markdown
---
default: minor
---

# Add `Strategy.ChasesFlip7`

Optional detail in Markdown below the heading. It becomes the changelog entry.
```

`default` is the only package name because the NuGet package and the terminal
app share one version. The type is `major`, `minor` or `patch`. While the
version is below 1.0, `major` bumps the middle number and both `minor` and
`patch` bump the last one, so breaking changes stay visible in the version.
